diff --git a/PlayerSync/Services/SourceQualityExport/README.md b/PlayerSync/Services/SourceQualityExport/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1c49c0a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PlayerSync/Services/SourceQualityExport/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# Source-quality export IPC (API version 1)
+
+Lets another plugin (the PlayerSync Mod Exporter) get the **original, source-quality files** behind one visible pair's
+current appearance for an explicitly started export, without changing how PlayerSync synchronizes.
+
+## What it does and does not do
+
+* Works only for a pair that is visible and not paused, chosen by its game object address.
+* Only files in that pair's current character data **after** PlayerSync's permission and filter rules (`Pair.GetSyncedCharacterDataCopy`,
+  the same `RemoveNotSyncedFiles` used before applying) are fetched. File swaps are never fetched. Anything else is reported `NotPermitted`
+  and never sent to the server.
+* Always uses the original hash, even when the server offers a compressed alternate (`AlwaysSourceQuality`). The user's
+  `TextureCompressionMode`, the Override UIDs list and the pair's applied appearance are not changed; normal synchronization keeps
+  following the configured policy (`FileDownloadManager.UsesCompressedAlternate`).
+* Reuses `FileDownloadManager`: the server metadata request (`GetFileInfoAsync`, which also records forbidden files in
+  `ForbiddenTransfers`), the authenticated download with its slots, speed limit and 404 reporting (`DownloadTransportFileAsync`), and the
+  transport decoding (`TransportCodec`: munge key and LZ4). There is no separate downloader.
+* Writes only into the caller's staging folder, which must exist and be outside PlayerSync's cache folder and Penumbra's mod folder.
+  Nothing is written to the cache, `FileCache.csv` is not touched, `PersistFileToStorage` is not called, and no cache file is moved,
+  rewritten or deleted. Originals already on this computer are hashed read-only and reported as `CachedOriginal` with their path.
+* Every downloaded file is decoded and its SHA-1 compared with the requested hash before it is kept.
+* Temporary files are always removed. On cancel, failure or plugin unload the job also removes the originals it staged. It never deletes
+  anything it did not create.
+* One request runs at a time, with at most 5000 files.
+
+## Functions
+
+| Name | Signature | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| `PlayerSync.SourceQualityExport.GetApiVersion` | `Func<int>` | `1` |
+| `PlayerSync.SourceQualityExport.Start` | `Func<nint, string, List<string>, string>` (address, staging folder, hashes) | `{"requestId": "..."}` or `{"error": "..."}` |
+| `PlayerSync.SourceQualityExport.GetStatus` | `Func<string, string>` (request id) | see below |
+| `PlayerSync.SourceQualityExport.Cancel` | `Func<string, bool>` | Cancels a running request (its files are deleted) and forgets it. For a finished request it only forgets it; the staged files stay for the caller. |
+
+Call `Start` on the framework thread.
+
+`GetStatus`:
+
+```json
+{"state": "Running|Completed|Cancelled|Failed|Unknown", "error": null,
+ "files": [{"hash": "...", "gamePath": "...", "status": "...", "path": "...", "size": 0, "sha1Verified": true, "message": null}]}
+```
+
+| `status` | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `Pending` | Not finished yet |
+| `CachedOriginal` | Already on this computer; `path` is the existing copy (read only) |
+| `Downloaded` | Downloaded, decoded and SHA-1 verified into the staging folder; `path` is the staged file |
+| `NotPermitted` | Not in the pair's permission-filtered data; not requested |
+| `Forbidden` | The file server forbids it |
+| `NotOnServer` | The file server no longer has the original |
+| `Unavailable` | The request or download failed |
+| `HashMismatch` | The decoded bytes did not match; nothing kept |
+| `Failed` | Could not be decoded, or invalid input |
+| `Cancelled` | The request was cancelled or failed as a whole |
+
+## Code
+
+* `PlayerSync/Services/SourceQualityExport/SourceQualityExportService.cs`: IPC, pair and permission checks, staging folder checks.
+* `PlayerSync/Services/SourceQualityExport/SourceQualityExportJob.cs`: the per-request work.
+* `PlayerSync/WebAPI/Files/FileDownloadManager.cs`: `UsesCompressedAlternate`, `GetFileInfoAsync`, `DownloadTransportFileAsync` (the existing
+  download paths call the same helpers; their behaviour is unchanged).
+* `PlayerSync/WebAPI/Files/TransportCodec.cs`: the munge and LZ4 decoding, shared by both paths.
+* `PlayerSync/PlayerData/Pairs/Pair.cs`: `GetSyncedCharacterDataCopy`.
+* Tests: `PlayerSync.SourceQualityExportTest`.
